# Errant Minion leaves the battlefield before its trigger resolves: with its trigger on the stack in Bot2's upkeep, Bot2 returns its
# enchanted Memnite to hand with Unsummon, and the Aura goes to its owner's graveyard. The trigger still resolves: Bot2 pays one mana,
# and the Aura deals the 2 damage as it last existed (CR 113.7a), 1 of it prevented - the prevention is of that damage, not of an
# object the Aura has stopped being (CR 608.2c, 615.7).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Errant Minion
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Unsummon
Island x20

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Errant Minion.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Unsummon.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Errant Minion; Black Lotus
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.PayCost(Times: 1)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Life = 20
